{#
  404 — Figma 295:11180 (1512 x 884).

  PERMALINK IS THE WHOLE WIRING. Vercel serves /404.html from the output root for
  any unmatched route on a static build, so this file needs no rule in
  vercel.json and does not interact with the three redirects committed there.

  nav: false — the comp's two 96px bands are EMPTY. No logo, no nav, no footer;
  the header rule-band is a frame, not the site header with its contents hidden.
  base.njk's flag drops it, which is why this page needs no layout of its own.

  THE ILLUSTRATION IS STATIC. It is the same character as the About section's,
  and that one follows the cursor with its eyes — this one deliberately does not.
  An error page that watches you is a joke that lands once and then reads as
  broken; the comp draws it looking away.

  BOTH ASSETS ARE <img>, INCLUDING THE SVG, and the title is the interesting one:
  404-title.svg bakes fill="#1A1A1A". That is --fig-ink, and this page's light
  scope sets --text-primary to --fig-black (#000000) — so inlining it through the
  inlineSvg filter the way the hero's "Designer" word is done would recolour it to
  pure black and miss the node by 26 levels on every channel. The filter exists
  for artwork that MUST inherit; this is artwork that must not.

  EVERYTHING IN BOTH COLUMNS IS CENTRED, which is not a simplification of the
  comp but a reading of it. The node gives the title y=178 inside a 692 banner and
  the button x=216 inside a 636 one; 692 minus the 336 of stacked content is 356,
  half of which is 178, and (636-204)/2 is exactly 216. The illustration is inset
  55.28 left and 55.27 right, 35 top and 35 bottom. Absolute offsets would restate
  those numbers; flex centring reproduces them and survives a font swap.
#}

{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}

